 {:name "require-model-invariants-to-link-enumerated-data-with-derived-counts"
  :lane :trajectory-lane
  :level :semantic-model-audit
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:hook
   "If a theorem moves from an analytic function to its zero count and then to an enumerated zero sequence, verify that the structure actually relates all three objects; separately well-typed fields can make the conclusion false."
   :how-to-apply
   ["Draw the dependency chain named by the informal proof: here `f → zeros of f → zeroCount → weighted summability`."
    "For every arrow, locate a structure field, definition, or proved invariant that enforces it."
    "Treat `True` analytic hypotheses, constant derived quantities, and freely chosen enumerations as independent warning signs."
    "Construct a model satisfying the retained fields while choosing the unconstrained field adversarially."
    "Require the intended linking invariant in `ProblemData` before proving downstream estimates; do not count consequences of a constant placeholder as progress on the intended theorem."]
   :observed-case
   {:problem "a01J06"
    :formal-shape
    ["`hEntire : True` does not constrain `f`."
     "`zeroCount data r := 0` does not count `data.zeros`."
     "`zeros : ℕ → ℂ` is not related to `f` or `zeroCount`."]
    :countermodel
    "Take the zero function and the constant-zero enumeration. The stub count has linear growth, but every weight is one, so the requested series is not summable."
    :verification
    "`unconstrainedZerosCounterexample_not_summable` is axiom-clean in commit `a8f8752a816746d24e6ce125e446385a7d12f0d1`."}
   :relation-to-existing
   {:memory-id
    "e-codexpilot-inspect-placeholder-definitions-before-claiming-mathematical-content"
    :distinction
    "The existing memory catches a central definition implemented as a constant. This record adds the structural case where independently meaningful fields lack the invariant that makes a downstream theorem about the same mathematical object."}
   :rule
   "Before proving a theorem over a bundled problem structure, audit that every semantic transition in the informal argument is represented by a formal invariant; type compatibility and axiom-clean helper proofs do not connect independent fields."
   :boundary
   "The countermodel refutes the current formal target. It does not refute the intended zero-distribution theorem once the missing entire-function, zero-enumeration, and counting invariants are supplied."
   :capture-kind :machine-checked-countermodel-to-unconstrained-formal-model}
